# IsoRim wild animals in the blob style (Deer stag + doe, Wild boar, Bear, Timber wolf). Generated by tools/make_wild1_concept.py
# (wild1 concept v1, 2026-11-09, not yet reviewed). Kd = the vanilla sprite's lit white.
# Deer (buck (156,112,62), doe (188,146,110), fawn (140,74,41)) and Bear (grizzly (112,82,65), polar (180,180,180)) take
# their coat colour from the game (ModelDef tintFromGraphic, Api 49). The deer's antlers and tail are plain materials,
# which tintFromGraphic leaves alone (vanilla's CutoutComplex mask leaves them untinted too).
# Wild boar and timber wolf: vanilla sprites are untinted, so their colours are baked into the textures (no tintFromGraphic).
newmtl an_deer_stag_blob
Kd 0.960 0.960 0.960
map_Kd IsoRim/Animals/DeerStag

newmtl an_deer_stag_blob_antler
Kd 0.721 0.670 0.505

newmtl an_deer_stag_blob_tail
Kd 0.960 0.960 0.960

newmtl an_deer_doe_blob
Kd 0.960 0.960 0.960
map_Kd IsoRim/Animals/DeerDoe

newmtl an_deer_doe_blob_tail
Kd 0.960 0.960 0.960

newmtl an_wildboar_blob
Kd 0.960 0.960 0.960
map_Kd IsoRim/Animals/WildBoar

newmtl an_bear_blob
Kd 0.960 0.960 0.960
map_Kd IsoRim/Animals/Bear

newmtl an_wolf_timber_blob
Kd 0.960 0.960 0.960
map_Kd IsoRim/Animals/WolfTimber

# Fawn (vanilla DeerBaby, both sexes in the first two life stages): animal_deer_fawn_blob.obj = the doe with spots (tools/make_deer_fawn.py);
# the fawn colour (140,74,41) is baked into DeerFawn.png and the white spots stay untinted (binding tint (255,255,255)).
newmtl an_deer_fawn_blob
Kd 0.960 0.960 0.960
map_Kd IsoRim/Animals/DeerFawn
